  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, confirming RNA is the dominant modality. However, we have only tested singleprofile for RNA, leaving the single-vs-multiprofile axis completely unexplored. This is a fundamental design choice that gates half the search space (all multiprofile and multimodal configurations). Config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the cleanest possible test: it changes only the profile setting and adds the simplest aggregation (avgpool) relative to config_001, isolating the effect of multiple profiles. If multiprofile+avgpool improves over 48.5%, it validates the multiprofile axis and motivates testing transformer aggregation (config_003) and multimodal extensions. If it does not improve, we can deprioritize all multiprofile configurations and focus budget on RNA encoder variation (scvi, scgpt) or image encoder upgrades. Under a tight budget, resolving this binary design question on the strongest modality with the simplest change maximizes information gain per experiment."
}

